INT. LAKESIDE CABIN - LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

A wood stove ticks. Six chairs around a worn table. A phone with a long cord hangs on the wall.

The Aldridge family gathers: father ROSCOE ALDRIDGE (60s), mother FRANCES ALDRIDGE (60s), their daughters CAMILLA (30s) and JOSEPHINE "JO" (28), and son LIAM (25). Nobody has taken off a coat.

The phone rings. Everyone looks at it. Frances rises, answers.

FRANCES
Hello?

DOCTOR (V.O.)
(through phone)
Mrs. Aldridge? It's Dr. Suarez at Mercy General.

FRANCES
Yes. Go ahead.

DOCTOR (V.O.)
(through phone)
I'm sorry. He didn't make it through the surgery.

Frances lowers the receiver. She stares at the wall.

ROSCOE
Frances?

She hangs up. Turns to the room.

FRANCES
It's Papa.

Camilla steps back, a hand pressed to her mouth. Jo bursts into tears; Liam puts an arm around her. Roscoe takes off his cap and holds it with both hands.

ROSCOE
Then we go to him.

CAMILLA
Tonight?

ROSCOE
Tonight.

Nobody moves. The stove ticks. Then Frances takes her purse from the table and opens the cabin door onto the dark lake.
